ABSTRACT

A3 defines what a plan is. A1 defines the FSM that executes it. A5 defines the gate that verifies each step. A6 defines how tiles are invoked. A7 defines how everything is logged.

None of these specify what happens when a step fails.

A plan with ten steps, where step seven is refused by VERIFY — what happens to steps one through six? Are they undone? Retried? Does execution halt? Who decides?

A8 answers these questions. It defines the runtime composition semantics — how sub-tasks sequence, how failure propagates, how recovery is bounded, and how escalation to humans is handled. Every rule is deterministic, every recovery is bounded, every path is logged.

Status: Specification. No reference implementation. No hardware validation. Machine verification pending.

