2. SUB-TASK MODEL

2.1 Definition

Definition 1 (Sub-Task). A sub-task is the atomic unit of plan execution:

```
sub_task = ⟨ sub_id, parent_plan, step_index, kind, payload, status, attempt ⟩
```

Field Type Description
sub_id Nat Unique identifier within a plan
parent_plan PlanID The plan this sub-task belongs to
step_index Nat Index in the plan's step sequence
kind SubTaskKind ACTION, PLAN, CONDITIONAL
payload Payload The action ID, plan ID, or predicate
status Status PENDING, RUNNING, SUCCESS, FAILED, REFUSED, ROLLED_BACK
attempt Nat Retry counter

2.2 Sub-Task Kind

Definition 2 (SubTaskKind). Three kinds, mirroring A3 §2.2:

Kind Payload Execution
ACTION ActionID Single action commit (A2)
PLAN PlanID Nested plan invocation (A6)
CONDITIONAL PredicateID Evaluate predicate; branch

2.3 Sub-Task Status

Definition 3 (Status). The status is one of:

Status Meaning Terminal?
PENDING Not yet started No
RUNNING In progress No
SUCCESS Committed successfully Yes
FAILED Error during execution Yes
REFUSED VERIFY refused the action Yes
ROLLED_BACK Rollback completed Yes

Once a sub-task reaches a terminal status, it does not change.

