3. THE SUB-TASK QUEUE

3.1 Definition

Definition 4 (Sub-Task Queue). DECOMPOSE (A3 §6) produces a bounded, ordered sequence of sub-tasks:

```
queue = ⟨ st_1, st_2, …, st_n ⟩
```

with n ≤ K × D_invoke (A3 §6.4).

3.2 Queue Properties

Property Meaning
Ordered Sub-tasks execute in declared order
Bounded n ≤ K × D_invoke
Finite Each sub-task is finite (A2, A3)
Single-threaded One sub-task runs at a time (A1 §6, A6 Rule P2)

3.3 Queue Consumption

Rule Q1 (Sequential Consumption). The FSM consumes sub-tasks one at a time, in order.

Rule Q2 (No Reordering). Sub-tasks are not reordered at runtime. Order is fixed by DECOMPOSE.

Rule Q3 (No Insertion). New sub-tasks are not inserted into the queue at runtime.

Rule Q4 (Bounded Retry). A sub-task may be retried in place (not re-enqueued), up to its declared retry policy.

These rules make the queue deterministic. Same plan, same state → same execution order.

