12. OPEN DESIGN TENSIONS

# Question Impact
1 Rollback semantics vs. non-recoverable actions. Some actions (e.g., firing a brake) cannot be undone. How does rollback handle them? Requires "non-reversible action" flag in A2 schema.
2 Retry policy per sub-task or per plan? Per sub-task is more granular; per plan is simpler. Affects ROM size and expressiveness.
3 Skip semantics for nested plans. Can a Skip apply to a whole nested plan, or only leaf actions? Affects failure propagation complexity.
4 Escalation return path. After escalation, how does the agent re-enter? Is there a re-entry protocol? Needs its own sub-spec if nontrivial.
5 Checkpoint frequency. Every COMMIT, or every N? Every COMMIT is expensive; every N is less precise. Trade-off.
6 Cross-plan rollback. Rule RB5 forbids it. Is this too restrictive for long-horizon plans? May need relaxation for multi-task agents.
7 Rollback and external effects. If an action changes the world (e.g., a robot moved), rollback restores internal state but not the world. Needs "world effect" annotation in A2 schema.
8 Deterministic retry futility. Given A8-R1, retries only help for environmental changes. How does the plan distinguish environmental from internal failures? Needs failure classification.

None are fatal. All must be resolved before A8 v2.0.

