APPENDIX A — Plain Language

What happens if a step in a plan fails?
The plan has rules for that. It might stop, retry, or go back to an earlier point.
Can the plan invent a new way to recover?
No. Only what was declared at burn time.
How many times can it retry?
As many as the plan allows. Then it stops.
Can it go back to an earlier point?
Yes. It reads the log, finds a saved moment, and restores from there.
Can it ask a human?
Yes. It writes a request and stops.
Can it try forever?
No. Everything is bounded. Total cycles, retries, rollbacks — all have limits.
What is this called?
A8 — composition and failure semantics.

